record legeos.evidence.bar-hover-row-previews-20260908/1 : evidence {
    title "The bar's hover row renders a window's capture with its title, falls back to the icon without one, and fits the island at 132 px an item"
    state superseded
    scope [
        path "shell/lege-shell/src/surface/bar_screen.rs",
        path "shell/lege-shell/src/surface/offscreen.rs",
        path "shell/lege-shell/src/taskbar.rs"
    ]
    result pass
    method command
    observed_at git:1d0340c20684f0854f32379c63762310c58bdc2e
    command "cargo test -p lege-shell"
    artifact "docs/measurements/bar-20260908f/bar-row.png"
    summary """
        390 tests pass (379 lib, 11 integration, 0 skipped). New: a_row_item_shows_its_window_preview_and_falls_back_without_one (the window with a capture shows its pixels; the one without shows its own painted fallback, not an empty box and not the other window's picture), the_open_row_fits_inside_the_island (every row rect inside island_width for 2- and 5-window entries, and the row never widens the surface), previews_are_asked_for_only_while_a_row_is_open (BarScreen::preview_wants is empty with no row, is exactly the open entry's windows while one is up, and is empty again after HOVER_CLOSE_MS). The row's item pitch went 220 -> 132 logical px and its band 40 -> 104: a three-window row is 396 px wide where it was 660, inside an island_width(3) of 716. The three existing bar-presence baseline hashes are unchanged, which is the check that nothing outside the row moved; a fourth case, bar-row, was hashed only after the dumped PNGs were read by eye.
        """
    derived_from [ @legeos.decision.one-persistent-bottom-bar-tags-not-bands ]
}

