record legeos.evidence.bar-lane-2-nested-fullscreen/1 : evidence {
    title "Nested lege-comp (winit on the X11 host) with lege-shell and a fullscreen kitty: every pixel of the 2560x1600 output, the bottom 48px bar zone included, is the client's opaque background — the fullscreen window takes Output::logical and stacks above the bar. With an 80%-opaque client the same strip reads exactly 0.2x the bar's ground (47,48,48 against 236,238,240), which is the bar still mapped and still painting underneath. Killing the client returns the bar (ground 236,238,240, a TAG_FILL chip at 46,51,61) with no bar re-creation in the shell log: the surface was never destroyed and its zone was never released."
    state verified
    result pass
    method observation
    observed_at git:6cb582adab19c168c47a7fd714878656abde7d66
    artifact "docs/measurements/bar-20260908/nested-fullscreen-covers-bar.png"
    summary """
        Nested lege-comp (winit on the X11 host) with lege-shell and a fullscreen kitty: every pixel of the 2560x1600 output, the bottom 48px bar zone included, is the client's opaque background — the fullscreen window takes Output::logical and stacks above the bar. With an 80%-opaque client the same strip reads exactly 0.2x the bar's ground (47,48,48 against 236,238,240), which is the bar still mapped and still painting underneath. Killing the client returns the bar (ground 236,238,240, a TAG_FILL chip at 46,51,61) with no bar re-creation in the shell log: the surface was never destroyed and its zone was never released.
        """
}

