record legeos.evidence.bar-over-home-not-observed-at-a-seat/1 : evidence {
    title "bar-over-home and fullscreen-is-uninterrupted were not observed: the nested session cannot start while the live one is up"
    state verified
    result inconclusive
    method observation
    observed_at git:0b6d8fc3c84e46d6a7458b511b621e3ae3ba9f48
    summary """
        Lane B could not run scripts/nested-session.sh: refuse_over_live_session declines while lege-sessiond.service and lege-comp.service are active, which they are (the user is logged into the installed session), and a nested session would fight it for org.legeos.Session on the shared user bus. So the observation-method checks bar-over-home and fullscreen-is-uninterrupted have no evidence from this lane. The shell side is unit-tested and rendered; the compositor side (contract Z1) is present in the tree - window_bridge::a_zero_zone_subtracts_nothing and protocols_shell::handle_set_exclusive_zone keep a claim of 0 rather than releasing it, and shell_surface_placement anchors a Bottom claim at the output's bottom edge with the surface's own height - but was read, not run at a seat. The exact hands-on lines are in .agent/scratch/bar-5/RUNBOOK-lane-B.md.
        """
}

