record legeos.evidence.bottom-edge-gates-20260908/1 : evidence {
    title "The bottom-edge work's four command gates pass at e6e1b1c3"
    state verified
    result pass
    method command
    observed_at git:e6e1b1c3523004f2eef22aa3bfd2dc2abae4a06a
    command "just check && cargo test -p lege-window a_window_that_fills_the_screen_has_no_frame && cargo test -p lege-window a_pinned_window_sorts_above_the_others_without_changing_layer && cargo test -p lege-shell the_switcher_hides_only_under_a_window_that_fills_the_screen"
    summary """
        `just check` exits 0 on the full gate, including check-assets and check-actions (23 CLI
        verbs all reach a subcommand, 71 surface-named actions all declared, 19 chorded actions all
        have a pointer route). The three focused tests pass: 1 passed each.

        One correction landed with this run. The #switcher-waits-and-returns check named
        `the_switcher_hides_under_a_window_that_fills_the_screen_and_comes_back_on_a_peek`, which
        does not exist. `cargo test -p lege-shell <that name>` reports "running 0 tests ... test
        result: ok. 0 passed; 0 failed; 373 filtered out" and exits 0, so the gate was passing
        without executing anything — a check that could not fail. The real test is
        `the_switcher_hides_only_under_a_window_that_fills_the_screen`
        (shell/lege-shell/src/surface/app.rs:4765), which does cover both the hide-under and the
        reveal-shows cases, and the check now names it.

        The two hands-on checks are deliberately not covered here: scripts/nested-session.sh refuses
        while the installed session is running, and the compositor half needs a logout.
        """
}

