record legeos.evidence.critical-grace-policy-accepted-20260909/1 : evidence {
    title "The user reviewed the behaviour change in session and delegated the call, saying they did not see what choice there was to make and trusted the judgement. Accepted: the emergency kill delay is now a property of the selected victim's instance identity rather than of the Critical episode. What changes is that a newly selected victim always gets the full checkpoint deadline before KillCgroup, so a long Critical episode whose victim keeps changing can terminate nothing for as long as the ranking keeps moving; what it removes is a victim being asked to checkpoint and killed on the same tick, having inherited an already-expired countdown. The governor stays observe-only under @legeos.constraint.identity-and-launch-safety, so the change is proven by replay, not on the live machine, and no user data was ever at risk from either behaviour."
    state verified
    result pass
    method manual
    observed_at git:b82906a2e82077f580c9b2111d4539a928d62d89
    summary """
        The user reviewed the behaviour change in session and delegated the call, saying they did not see what choice there was to make and trusted the judgement. Accepted: the emergency kill delay is now a property of the selected victim's instance identity rather than of the Critical episode. What changes is that a newly selected victim always gets the full checkpoint deadline before KillCgroup, so a long Critical episode whose victim keeps changing can terminate nothing for as long as the ranking keeps moving; what it removes is a victim being asked to checkpoint and killed on the same tick, having inherited an already-expired countdown. The governor stays observe-only under @legeos.constraint.identity-and-launch-safety, so the change is proven by replay, not on the live machine, and no user data was ever at risk from either behaviour.
        """
}

