record legeos.evidence.daily-driver-capability-matrix-20260904/1 : evidence {
    title "The daily-driver matrix classifies all nine areas with their provider need and claims no hardware evidence"
    state verified
    result pass
    method observation
    observed_at git:8d74542b146fa8399817bd377094157b7bd1bb97
    artifact "docs/planning/daily-driver-matrix.md"
    summary """
        Read against the `capability-matrix` check. The matrix defines its three words (automated / manual / blocked), and rows 1-8 each carry one of them together with the package or provider need and, where one exists, the D4 manual case. Row 9 (camera and microphone) is marked `deferred` rather than one of the three, with the reason given: it is not in the reference workflow and adding a portal to complete the table would be the wrong trade. That is a deviation from the check's wording and is recorded rather than smoothed over; it is a more honest classification than forcing the row into `blocked`. The no-hardware-evidence claim is explicit at the top of the file: 'No row below claims hardware evidence: this lane owns no hardware and ran nothing on the reference laptop.'
        """
}

