record legeos.evidence.progressive-snapshots.summary-vs-materialized/1 : evidence {
    title "Summary snapshot is 1247x smaller and 17.9x faster than materialized on a build-directory fixture"
    state verified
    result pass
    method command
    observed_at git:857efe4b21008ace84a6a89b85b9cd3020bae665
    command "cargo test -p lege-file-index --release -- --ignored --nocapture progressive_snapshot_benchmark"
    artifact "docs/measurements/progressive-snapshots-2026-09-04.md"
    summary """
        SnapshotRequest gained detail: SnapshotDetail{Materialized,Summary}, subtree: Option<NativePath>, and include_coverage: Vec<Coverage>, all additive #[serde(default)] JSON fields on the frozen OpenSnapshot signature (184 members unchanged per check-interface-signatures). On a 5000-file src/ + 20000-file target/-shaped Opaque fixture, Summary mode measured 580 bytes / 0.314ms vs Materialized's 723252 bytes / 5.625ms -- 1247x smaller, 17.9x faster. A smaller 500+500 fixture (permanent test, runs under just check) measured 123.7x. Any field mask reaching outside the original 8 fields (COVERAGE, AGGREGATE) stamps a new FORMAT_EXTENDED=2; SnapshotReader rejects an unrecognised format outright.
        """
}

record legeos.evidence.progressive-snapshots.treemap-adapter/1 : evidence {
    title "Treemap TreeSource adapter matches a direct scan; shell no longer always walks the disk"
    state verified
    result pass
    method command
    observed_at git:857efe4b21008ace84a6a89b85b9cd3020bae665
    command "cargo test -p lege-client --lib tree_source"
    artifact "crates/lege-client/src/tree_source.rs"
    summary """
        crates/lege-client/src/tree_source.rs introduces the POR §4.3 TreeSource trait, DirectScanSource (the pre-existing lege_treemap::scan, unchanged, kept as the explicit fallback), and an index-snapshot path (load_snapshot_tree) that rebases OpenSnapshot to the requested subtree in Materialized detail. A hermetic in-process test (no D-Bus, no lege-filed) proves the adapter produces the same RawEntry rows, sorted, as a direct scan of the same fixture. shell/lege-shell/src/surface/app.rs's spawn_treemap now tries the snapshot path first (async, via crate::data::session()) and falls back to DirectScanSource via spawn_blocking only when no service answers -- the walk at app.rs:2838 (lege_treemap::scan on every file tray redraw) is now the explicit fallback, not the only path. lege-treemap itself gained no new dependencies (deps-check still reports 0 transitive deps); the adapter lives in lege-client.
        """
}

