record legeos.evidence.templaros-medium-built-and-booted-20260909/1 : evidence {
    title "The first medium carrying the Templar name. 21 native packages built in an Ubuntu 26.04 chroot at c2403fa as set 0.1.0~dev1788945442+gc2403fa.dirty, published and verified into a fresh archive so no legeos-named set shares its index; a 4.37 GB ISO (sha256 aae24d622428a1c4333adb9b73564cc29bcf1f07ba77988953350ed046a488ee) carrying 1522 packages, 15 native and 1507 inherited, with templaros-shell, templaros-comp and templaros-desktop alongside papirus-icon-theme. iso-qemu.sh: OK under Secure-Boot OVMF with KVM — shim to GRUB to kernel, live userspace reached, preflight network pass. The bootstrap assembled on the build volume rather than in tmpfs and the machine held 25 GiB available throughout, where the 2026-09-07 build left it with 268 MB."
    state verified
    result pass
    method command
    observed_at git:c2403fa22668d545a1d73bf6bcd64b274b64e6c5
    command "tests/integration/iso-qemu.sh"
    artifact "docs/measurements/iso-build-templar-20260909.txt"
    summary """
        The first medium carrying the Templar name. 21 native packages built in an Ubuntu 26.04 chroot at c2403fa as set 0.1.0~dev1788945442+gc2403fa.dirty, published and verified into a fresh archive so no legeos-named set shares its index; a 4.37 GB ISO (sha256 aae24d622428a1c4333adb9b73564cc29bcf1f07ba77988953350ed046a488ee) carrying 1522 packages, 15 native and 1507 inherited, with templaros-shell, templaros-comp and templaros-desktop alongside papirus-icon-theme. iso-qemu.sh: OK under Secure-Boot OVMF with KVM — shim to GRUB to kernel, live userspace reached, preflight network pass. The bootstrap assembled on the build volume rather than in tmpfs and the machine held 25 GiB available throughout, where the 2026-09-07 build left it with 268 MB.
        """
}

