record legeos.evidence.the-bottom-edge-reviewed-and-its-seven-findings/1 : evidence {
    title "The Fable advisor's round on the bottom-edge change: seven findings, all fixed"
    state verified
    result pass
    method manual
    observed_at git:38b16d59ac2fc0f27d7bdaf86eacb5dc6e744229
    summary """
        Seven defects, six of them consequences of a screen-filling window's tag strip being drawn over its own client area where a framed window's is drawn beside it: the tag gap fell through to the window behind; every affordance press was delivered to the client as well; covering_chrome was filtered on read and so could never be cleared, bringing the strip back with no dwell on the next maximize; the peek band is the strip's own bottom ten pixels, so aiming at the close tag opened the switcher under it; a click nudged the window three pixels; the covering window was found without asking whether it was visible; and the machine cluster was destroyed with no home_revealed term and no way back. Two judgement calls taken from the same review: the peek enters the shell's own reveal rather than bypassing it, so one gesture has one way out; and the cluster returns on the peek. All seven fixed at 38b16d5, gate green, 1999 tests.
        """
}

record legeos.evidence.the-cluster-split-reviewed-and-its-eight-findings/1 : evidence {
    title "A second adversarial review of the cluster split and the fullscreen chrome found eight issues; all eight were fixed. Four existed only with a real pointer and a real compositor and no test could have caught them: chips sliding out from under the pointer when a row widened the surface, a stale surface-local pointer after a bottom-anchored resize, an account popover with no dismissal route because its ground click landed outside the input region, and a cluster that never redrew for its own clock. The gate is green after all of them."
    state verified
    result pass
    method command
    observed_at git:1792fab6398121a27a9d562525987a008e8a314e
    command "just check"
    artifact ".agent/scratch/bar-6/advisor-findings-2.md"
    summary """
        A second adversarial review of the cluster split and the fullscreen chrome found eight issues; all eight were fixed. Four existed only with a real pointer and a real compositor and no test could have caught them: chips sliding out from under the pointer when a row widened the surface, a stale surface-local pointer after a bottom-anchored resize, an account popover with no dismissal route because its ground click landed outside the input region, and a cluster that never redrew for its own clock. The gate is green after all of them.
